# Kani runs each wrapper on a real atomic, one thread (src/kani/atomic.rs).
# loom and C11 (the weak-memory half, verus/WEAKMEM.md): every access to a
# counter after it is moved into place goes through these wrappers
# (tests/loom/tests/access.rs: arena.rs names the bound counts and the
# arena count, and policy.rs the position, only in vspec/count.rs calls
# and ghost lines, and moves a count into place raw only where it was
# minted, in `Arenas::put_head` and `put_entry`; this file mints one
# CountPerm per atomic, in `new`, and no `const` item copies one), so a
# permission's value reads as the last write in its atomic's modification
# order. C++20 orders one atomic's writes in one modification order
# consistent with happens-before ([intro.races]); a read-modify-write
# reads the last value before its own write, for every ordering
# ([atomics.order] p10): `fetch_add`, `fetch_sub`, `swap` and a successful
# `compare_exchange` (the strong form, which fails only when the values
# differ); a load, or a failed `compare_exchange`, reads a write no older
# than the last one that happens before it (coherence), so it returns the
# permission's value at its place in that order. `BoundPred` and
# `FracPred` each name one atomic and ghost state only, so they need no
# ordering across locations, but that an `unbind`'s `fetch_sub` comes
# after the `fetch_add` that minted its ticket: the thread that unbinds
# reads the heap's plain `bound` and `arena`, written when it was bound,
# which a race-free program orders after the binding. `NarenasPred` also
# holds the table entries' permissions and the built arenas, which the
# count's `Release` store and `Acquire` loads publish (a release/acquire
# pair, [atomics.order] p2).
# The count, narenas and position models check these consequences on
# copies of the callers' steps (tests/loom/tests/pins.rs).
fetch_add	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::count_fetch_add, and loom: count::loom_count_bind_assign_unbind and count::loom_count_try_bind_idle_rival; not checked: this body under concurrency, which the models replace with loom's `fetch_add` inside copies of the `Arenas` steps, in the configurations tests/loom/src/count.rs states; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the counter's last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)
fetch_sub	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::count_fetch_sub, and loom: count::loom_count_bind_assign_unbind and count::loom_count_try_bind_idle_rival; not checked: this body under concurrency, which the models replace with loom's `fetch_sub` inside copies of the `Arenas` steps, in the configurations tests/loom/src/count.rs states; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the counter's last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)
store	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::count_store, and loom: narenas::loom_narenas_create_publishes; not checked: this body under concurrency, which the model replaces with loom's `store` inside copies of the `Arenas` steps, in the configuration tests/loom/src/narenas.rs states; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the counter's last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)
load	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::count_load, and loom: count::loom_count_bind_assign_unbind, narenas::loom_narenas_create_publishes and position::loom_position_apply_swaps; not checked: this body under concurrency, which the models replace with loom's `load` inside copies of the `Arenas` and `Policy` steps, in the configurations their files state; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the counter's last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)
swap	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::count_swap, and loom: position::loom_position_apply_swaps; not checked: this body under concurrency, which the model replaces with loom's `swap` inside copies of the `Policy` steps, in the configuration tests/loom/src/position.rs states; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the counter's last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)
compare_exchange	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::count_compare_exchange, and loom: count::loom_count_try_bind_idle_rival and count::loom_count_try_bind_idle_one_wins; not checked: this body under concurrency, which the models replace with loom's `compare_exchange` inside copies of the `Arenas` steps, in the configurations tests/loom/src/count.rs states; that it never fails spuriously, which loom's compare-and-swap cannot show (it has no spurious failure) and rests on `core`'s documentation of the strong form; the C11 argument above, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)
